        "answer": "Yes. The Host exposes client-callable entry points by decorating Host service methods with @Remote; each decorated method becomes callable from a plugin's client half through the generated ctx.remote.<service>.<method> namespace. ctx.remote.commands.execute is exactly the @Remote-decorated commands.execute(agent, line, submittedAttachments, signal): Promise<CommandExecution | undefined> above, which parses and runs a slash command on the Host without sending it to the model (and logs command/run + command/done). commands.list is the matching read-side Remote. The Host catalog also shows typertGateway.invoke(request: InvokeRemoteRequest): Promise<unknown> as the generic gateway that dispatches these Remote calls."
